msgid "def name(): starts a function. Its indented block runs only when you call name().\n\nParameters make it flexible: def build_row(y): can build on any row. return hands a result back and ends the function.\n\nGood names make the main loop read like a to-do list: collect_all(), build_plan(), wait(1)."
